WEBVTT

01:08.735 --> 01:09.736
Issue this.

01:11.738 --> 01:13.323
But what about the fireworks?

01:15.117 --> 01:16.159
Do it.

01:24.251 --> 01:25.252
Hey, Ruth.

01:27.379 --> 01:29.423
I'm gonna need you here today.

01:30.340 --> 01:32.843
Absolutely. I just need to leave at 3:00.

01:33.343 --> 01:36.763
No. That is exactly what I mean. Okay.

01:39.725 --> 01:42.019
This is insane,
you can't just lock me in here.

01:42.769 --> 01:44.479
I don't have time to relitigate this.

01:44.563 --> 01:47.816
I'm gonna be gone for 30 minutes.
You need a snack, ask Ruth.

01:50.777 --> 01:53.488
I can see you calculating how much
you think you can get away with

01:53.572 --> 01:56.366
in 30 minutes. So how about this,
I'm gonna call every ten.

01:57.951 --> 01:59.244
What do I do? Do I just…

02:00.120 --> 02:03.749
I press a button and then, like…

02:03.832 --> 02:05.959
How… What… How do I… What's the system?

02:06.585 --> 02:08.586
The system is you pick up
the goddamn phone.

02:08.669 --> 02:10.672
I didn't know we were swearing now.

02:11.673 --> 02:14.343
Hey, is it true that Reverend Bryce
hung himself?

02:17.054 --> 02:18.180
Wasn't he your friend?

02:24.770 --> 02:26.605
We'll talk about it when I get back.

02:47.209 --> 02:51.296
I don't get it. I saw him
at The Rye just a few weeks ago.

02:52.005 --> 02:53.674
He was getting a coffee.

02:54.925 --> 02:56.009
I think.

02:56.760 --> 02:58.804
Maybe not. We didn't talk.

02:59.555 --> 03:01.598
I didn't really know him anyway.

03:07.354 --> 03:08.647
Thank you, Paul.

03:09.439 --> 03:13.861
Once again, I'd like to remind everyone
that it is not mandatory that you speak.

03:38.886 --> 03:39.970
There's nothing.

03:41.763 --> 03:43.140
There's always something.

03:44.558 --> 03:46.310
What the hell happened here?

03:46.393 --> 03:48.145
And why would he burn everything?

03:48.228 --> 03:50.606
Just save every scrap you can.

03:54.776 --> 03:55.777
All right.

03:55.861 --> 03:58.989
Need to tell people what's going on
or they're gonna start getting killed.

04:01.658 --> 04:03.911
- I'm trying to get things under control.
- Yep.

04:03.994 --> 04:08.081
Your little curfew isn't gonna do it.
You can't even control your own son.

04:08.165 --> 04:10.334
Okay. Okay. Okay.

04:14.922 --> 04:15.923
All right.

04:32.147 --> 04:33.482
What's wrong?

04:36.985 --> 04:37.986
He…

04:38.070 --> 04:39.571
He tried to call me.

04:44.201 --> 04:45.494
And another number.

04:47.788 --> 04:48.789
A lot.

04:48.872 --> 04:49.873
Dial it.

05:01.760 --> 05:02.886
Hello?

05:04.847 --> 05:06.056
Hi. Yes…

05:08.100 --> 05:09.434
Who is this?

05:09.518 --> 05:10.686
Who is this?

05:11.395 --> 05:12.855
Sorry. I just…

05:13.355 --> 05:16.191
I found your number in my phone, and I--

05:16.275 --> 05:17.484
Fuck.

05:20.195 --> 05:21.405
You try.

05:21.905 --> 05:23.532
- Yes!
- He won't pick up.

05:23.615 --> 05:25.158
The call's coming from the same number.

05:27.286 --> 05:28.495
Hello?

05:28.579 --> 05:29.705
Hi. How are you?

05:30.873 --> 05:32.040
Good.

05:35.711 --> 05:37.379
Reverend Bryce gave me your number.

05:38.046 --> 05:39.673
Would you like an appointment?

05:40.632 --> 05:42.551
- Yes.
- Yes I would.

05:43.051 --> 05:44.303
Give me fifteen minutes.

05:45.429 --> 05:46.847
That's… Okay. Where are you?

05:51.268 --> 05:52.269
12 Birch Street.

06:07.367 --> 06:08.368
Come in!

06:21.089 --> 06:22.090
Hey.

06:29.723 --> 06:30.724
Thank you.

06:36.897 --> 06:37.898
This feels good.

06:42.319 --> 06:43.320
Okay.

06:51.286 --> 06:52.287
What's it gonna be?

07:06.552 --> 07:07.678
Who we got here?

07:13.809 --> 07:15.102
Hello again.

07:16.436 --> 07:18.355
That is a brutal fucking ride.

07:18.438 --> 07:19.606
Damn, Papa.

07:23.277 --> 07:24.278
Todd O'Connor?

07:25.320 --> 07:26.738
Hey, Patty. How you doin'?

07:26.822 --> 07:27.990
Yeah. Good thanks.

07:28.532 --> 07:31.243
- Oh, my God. You're a drug dealer.
- No, no. No, please.

07:31.326 --> 07:32.327
I'm a shaman.

07:32.828 --> 07:34.037
Is that cocaine?

07:34.121 --> 07:35.122
Yes.

07:36.331 --> 07:38.417
Todd and I went to school together.
We were like--

07:38.500 --> 07:40.002
What are… What are these?

07:40.085 --> 07:44.923
That, my friend, is the one fucking
mushroom I'm not going near.

07:45.007 --> 07:48.135
Dude, that shit is gonna take you
where you gotta go,

07:48.218 --> 07:50.804
regardless of if you wanna go there.

07:50.888 --> 07:52.806
Old timers call that thing Truesight.

07:53.473 --> 07:55.225
Only grows here local on the island.

07:55.309 --> 07:57.227
Imagine getting LASIK for your third eye.

07:57.311 --> 07:58.896
Blasts that thing open.

07:58.979 --> 07:59.980
Pow!

08:01.940 --> 08:06.862
I'm sorry, I'm trying to figure out
why Reverend Bryce would take it?

08:06.945 --> 08:08.363
Well, he was looking for answers.

08:08.447 --> 08:09.531
He hung himself.

08:12.326 --> 08:13.327
Shit.

08:18.290 --> 08:20.292
I guess he didn't like the answers.

08:21.293 --> 08:22.294
Damn.

08:22.794 --> 08:24.922
You know, I have a buddy who took it.

08:25.005 --> 08:26.298
You remember Brian Morrison?

08:26.381 --> 08:28.217
"Bri Guy"?
Stole his mom's car in eighth grade?

08:28.300 --> 08:30.511
Flipped it in the woods? Maniac.

08:30.594 --> 08:34.306
Anyway, Brian saw something on his trip
that changed him completely.

08:34.890 --> 08:37.392
He encountered something
he wouldn't talk about.

08:37.476 --> 08:40.187
But he chilled out majorly afterwards.

08:40.270 --> 08:43.232
Stopped getting into fights,
stopped yelling at his girl.

08:44.149 --> 08:45.526
She had to feed him though.

08:45.609 --> 08:47.611
He lost some pretty major motor skills.

08:48.612 --> 08:49.696
Happy guy though.

08:50.781 --> 08:52.908
Just hard for her
to get him down at night.

08:52.991 --> 08:59.331
Anyway, he drew the same thing
over, and over, and over again.

08:59.414 --> 09:02.835
I think he saw it on his trip.
I have one of them, lying around here.

09:04.419 --> 09:06.797
It's kinda ancient…

09:07.965 --> 09:10.676
vaguely religious iconography.

09:10.759 --> 09:14.096
It's the kind of sacred geometry
you don't just riff.

09:19.101 --> 09:20.102
Yeah, man.

09:20.811 --> 09:22.062
Yeah, take that in.

09:24.147 --> 09:26.275
- Some doors are meant to stay shut.
- Oh, yeah.

09:26.358 --> 09:27.609
Am I right, folks?

09:28.360 --> 09:29.444
How do you take it?

09:31.071 --> 09:34.533
Well, I can make you a tincture
for 35 bucks, if that's amenable?

09:34.616 --> 09:36.702
- No, thanks.
- You and your companions can hang out

09:36.785 --> 09:38.453
in the Peace Center
at no extra cost to you.

09:38.537 --> 09:39.538
Do it.

09:41.957 --> 09:43.125
Okay.

09:43.834 --> 09:45.335
Would you excuse us for a minute?

09:45.419 --> 09:48.380
Yeah, yeah. There's no rush
to the augmentation of the soul, folks.

09:48.922 --> 09:51.175
This fungus doesn't hold the secrets
of the island.

09:51.258 --> 09:52.885
It's gonna leave you muttering
in a corner.

09:52.968 --> 09:55.304
Look, if you don't want to take
the scary mushroom,

09:55.387 --> 09:57.723
after bringing all these tourists here
to the island,

09:57.806 --> 09:59.850
that's for you to live with.

10:14.156 --> 10:15.240
Wyck will take it.

10:16.325 --> 10:17.326
Very cool.

10:18.035 --> 10:19.786
No. Of course there's not gonna be
fireworks.

10:19.870 --> 10:21.788
Which part of "curfew"
do they not understand?

10:21.872 --> 10:25.042
Listen, I think you should know
that people are angry.

10:25.125 --> 10:29.296
Apparently Kurt is gathering a meeting.
Trying to overturn your curfew.

10:30.214 --> 10:31.715
I'll be back in 15 minutes.

10:33.258 --> 10:34.551
Damn it.

10:36.887 --> 10:38.305
- I've gotta get back.
- Uh-huh.

10:38.388 --> 10:39.640
I'll stay with him.

10:39.723 --> 10:42.643
- You sure you wanna do this?
- The only way out is through.

10:42.726 --> 10:44.728
I know, but it's jus… I don't know.

10:44.811 --> 10:47.898
Oh, God. It even looks hideous.

10:48.690 --> 10:50.275
But you can't taste it, right?

10:50.359 --> 10:51.360
What?

10:58.742 --> 11:01.620
It… it's in here?

11:07.292 --> 11:10.921
We said Wyck was gonna take it.

11:11.004 --> 11:12.256
Yeah. You're Wyck.

11:13.882 --> 11:17.469
- Oh, my God. Oh, my God!
- It's okay, it's okay.

11:17.553 --> 11:20.472
- Just sip it slowly.
- What? I finished it!

11:20.556 --> 11:23.183
I can't be on this! I can't be on this!

11:23.267 --> 11:24.726
Not now! Now today!

11:24.810 --> 11:26.061
Make yourself throw up.

11:26.144 --> 11:27.187
- I can't!
- Stay calm.

11:27.271 --> 11:30.357
- It's only a 12 hour experience.
- Oh, my God!

11:30.440 --> 11:31.567
- Oh, my God!
- Tom…

11:31.650 --> 11:33.777
Oh, my God. Oh, my God.

11:33.861 --> 11:35.487
It really is best to purge!

11:38.323 --> 11:39.741
I can't throw up. I've never been able to.

11:39.825 --> 11:42.202
- Here.
- Stop, stop!

11:42.286 --> 11:43.871
Come on, Tom. Shush!

11:43.954 --> 11:45.372
Stop, stop, stop, stop!

11:46.290 --> 11:47.749
Oh, my God. Evan.

11:48.625 --> 11:50.002
What am I gonna do about Evan?

11:50.586 --> 11:52.171
Don't worry. I'm on it.

11:53.088 --> 11:54.590
What? What are you gonna do?

11:59.261 --> 12:00.971
Careful here. Okay.

12:01.054 --> 12:03.515
And we're just gonna wind down here
in the Peace Center.

12:05.100 --> 12:06.310
That's good.

12:06.393 --> 12:09.438
Let's have a seat. On the mindfulness bed.

12:09.521 --> 12:11.190
Per… yeah. That's it. Yep.

12:11.273 --> 12:13.567
And let's get fully supine. Yep.

12:13.650 --> 12:16.278
And here we go.

12:18.488 --> 12:20.532
I'm so sorry.
I didn't realize she'd gotten out.

12:20.616 --> 12:21.992
Come here, Bridget.

12:22.075 --> 12:25.120
She's turning 50 soon,
so she's got wanderlust.

12:25.704 --> 12:28.498
Tom. Tom! Listen to me.

12:28.582 --> 12:30.125
Listen to me. Sit. Sit.

12:30.751 --> 12:33.921
Now, don't squander this.

12:34.505 --> 12:36.590
You find those answers, now.

12:36.673 --> 12:37.674
- What?
- Yeah.

12:38.342 --> 12:39.343
Good news.

12:40.302 --> 12:43.347
Evan is fine, and he's gonna stay
at Ruth's.

12:43.430 --> 12:44.932
Thank God. Who'd you talk to?

12:45.015 --> 12:46.558
- Evan.
- Oh, my God.

12:46.642 --> 12:48.018
- I have to get back.
- Tom.

12:48.101 --> 12:51.104
I think we just ride it out here.
He seems to know what he's doing.

12:51.188 --> 12:53.440
- Yeah.
- Don't you think it's best to stay here?

12:53.524 --> 12:56.276
Absolutely. I do personally have to go.

12:56.360 --> 12:58.028
As my girlfriend's cat has absconded.

12:58.111 --> 13:00.030
But in the meantime
you can totally guide him.

13:00.113 --> 13:01.740
- What?
- Just stay calm.

13:01.823 --> 13:05.661
And whatever you do, do not look
at any mirrors.

13:05.744 --> 13:07.079
You got this, Wyck.

13:09.373 --> 13:12.084
What do I do if you freak-out?
What do I do if you freak-out?

13:12.167 --> 13:13.710
Take me back to the office right now.

13:13.794 --> 13:17.256
- Have you seen anything?
- Take me back to the office. Now.

13:21.009 --> 13:22.636
Just stop yelling at me.

13:24.179 --> 13:25.305
How did we get here?

13:25.389 --> 13:26.515
Where's Wyck?

13:27.349 --> 13:28.809
You told him he could go.

13:29.393 --> 13:31.270
He said he was gonna find the answers
you won't.

13:31.353 --> 13:33.814
I don't know what that means but…

13:34.314 --> 13:35.315
Do you hear that?

13:42.531 --> 13:44.157
Just give me a name, Tom.

13:44.783 --> 13:47.369
Where's Evan? Where is my son?

13:48.579 --> 13:49.705
For the third time.

13:51.957 --> 13:53.000
Evan is not here.

13:54.376 --> 13:56.336
But we're gonna find him.

13:57.087 --> 13:58.547
Who's that kid he runs with?

13:59.631 --> 14:00.632
PJ Glanville?

14:00.716 --> 14:02.843
PJ Glanville is an awful, awful…

14:04.469 --> 14:05.470
boy.

14:08.932 --> 14:10.100
Do you hear that sound?

14:10.893 --> 14:13.854
No, Tom. I don't hear the sound.

14:14.354 --> 14:16.732
Just take a deep breath.

14:20.277 --> 14:21.653
What's wrong with him?

14:22.988 --> 14:25.073
Nothing. He's just…

14:25.616 --> 14:27.534
Here. Hold your organizer.

14:27.618 --> 14:29.995
He doesn't know how dangerous
it is out there.

14:31.371 --> 14:33.498
Patricia, he does… Can you hear me?

14:33.582 --> 14:35.417
He doesn't know how dangerous
it is out there!

14:36.835 --> 14:37.920
Hi, there.

14:38.003 --> 14:39.254
Oh, God!

14:42.508 --> 14:44.468
You girls gotta be careful around here.

14:44.551 --> 14:45.802
- Why?
- Why?

14:47.471 --> 14:49.681
The house there. The…

14:49.765 --> 14:52.392
Back in the day these girls
used to get these hang up calls.

14:55.020 --> 14:57.606
And turns out it was coming from the guy
who lived here.

14:57.689 --> 15:01.360
He, like, lost his mind,

15:01.443 --> 15:05.280
and one night just went out
and stabbed a bunch of bitches.

15:05.364 --> 15:07.241
Bitches? Really?

15:07.324 --> 15:09.576
Sorry, your majesty,
he stabbed a bunch of young women.

15:10.077 --> 15:11.078
Thank you.

15:11.161 --> 15:12.162
I'm serious. They…

15:12.246 --> 15:16.375
My uncle told me they tried to kill him.
I guess they called him the Boogeyman.

15:16.458 --> 15:19.127
And they shot him and he wouldn't die.

15:19.211 --> 15:20.212
And so they…

15:21.755 --> 15:23.715
they, like, buried him in the basement

15:23.799 --> 15:25.968
and they sealed the whole thing
in concrete.

15:26.051 --> 15:27.344
- Is he being serious?
- Yeah.

15:27.427 --> 15:29.763
You gotta be quiet around here,
you don't know…

15:31.431 --> 15:32.975
you don't know what's gonna happen.

15:39.648 --> 15:41.567
Jesus Christ, dude!

15:41.650 --> 15:42.693
- Jesus Christ!
- God!

15:42.776 --> 15:43.902
- Sorry.
- What's wrong with you?

15:43.986 --> 15:45.737
- Oh, my God.
- Okay, guys, we can be friends,

15:45.821 --> 15:48.198
and we can smoke pot, and we can make
each other laugh, you know?

15:48.282 --> 15:51.243
Okay. Well, just let me know
if he turns up.

15:51.326 --> 15:52.411
Thank you so much.

15:54.288 --> 15:55.289
She was nice.

15:57.207 --> 15:58.500
Oh, God.

16:02.296 --> 16:03.505
Were you gonna tell me?

16:05.841 --> 16:06.925
The curfew?

16:07.426 --> 16:10.262
See, I've got a cell that holds six,

16:10.345 --> 16:14.057
so when I go out tonight and see literally
everyone walking around,

16:14.141 --> 16:17.519
which I will,
because there are fireworks tonight,

16:17.603 --> 16:19.730
which six people do you
want me to pick up?

16:21.899 --> 16:24.109
Talk me through that.
Tell me how you see that happening.

16:27.029 --> 16:29.615
Okay, so I can see you've given this
a lot of thought. Okay, good.

16:29.698 --> 16:31.283
Patricia, come on.

16:31.366 --> 16:32.701
We're going down to the station.

16:32.784 --> 16:34.578
Me? Why?

16:34.661 --> 16:36.622
Well, I gotta take down your statement.

16:38.415 --> 16:40.334
- Can it wait?
- No, it cannot,

16:40.417 --> 16:44.296
because some people who woke up
in the sea last night wanna press charges.

16:45.464 --> 16:46.590
Okay, okay.

16:47.799 --> 16:51.178
I guess I'll be right back,
so you just sit here.

16:52.012 --> 16:53.013
Right?

16:56.058 --> 16:57.100
Don't open the door.

17:23.377 --> 17:24.377
Ger.

17:25.295 --> 17:27.256
Wyck. What are you doing here?

17:27.756 --> 17:29.091
- Something wrong?
- No.

17:29.174 --> 17:32.678
No, I'm working with the mayor
on something and I…

17:33.971 --> 17:36.557
I was wondering if I could get
your eye on it?

17:36.640 --> 17:38.058
You're working with the mayor?

17:38.141 --> 17:39.852
- Well, that's new.
- Yeah.

17:39.935 --> 17:41.687
I don't like it either, but…

17:42.980 --> 17:44.690
You think you could take a look? It's…

17:45.190 --> 17:46.650
- Yeah.
- It's important.

17:46.733 --> 17:47.734
Of course, yeah.

17:47.818 --> 17:49.820
Found it in Bryce's rectory.

17:50.404 --> 17:51.405
Yeah.

17:51.488 --> 17:52.489
Okay.

17:57.035 --> 17:58.036
Yeah.

17:59.079 --> 18:00.080
How have you been?

18:01.039 --> 18:02.040
Fine.

18:03.458 --> 18:06.837
Okay. Saving it for the memoir, I see.

18:08.589 --> 18:13.802
My father used to say
that you were too chatty.

18:17.472 --> 18:18.891
Yeah, he never liked me.

18:18.974 --> 18:21.310
Well, you kept me out too late.

18:22.352 --> 18:23.353
That's interesting.

18:23.437 --> 18:25.147
- Let me put it on the…
- Yeah.

18:27.149 --> 18:28.150
Put on the light.

18:31.486 --> 18:32.821
- Okay.
- All right.

18:33.989 --> 18:35.240
All right.

18:35.324 --> 18:38.243
"I do not comprehend the nature
of the curse

18:38.327 --> 18:40.787
that has fallen on the island.

18:41.330 --> 18:45.125
I do know that its heart beats
inside the cylinder

18:45.626 --> 18:48.045
that my husband wears around his neck.

18:48.128 --> 18:53.091
Who will crush my throat?
His hands? This plague?

18:53.175 --> 18:57.596
Death comes for each of us,
but I fear to me first.

18:57.679 --> 18:59.973
I know not how, but who.

19:01.099 --> 19:05.312
Of course, he's here with me,
so I say all of this in jest,

19:05.395 --> 19:07.272
and with that, I retire."

19:09.691 --> 19:10.692
That's…

19:12.194 --> 19:13.195
No.

19:23.830 --> 19:25.040
Tom?

19:27.125 --> 19:28.252
Are you okay?

19:30.879 --> 19:33.298
- I have to stop him.
- I have to stop him.

19:34.049 --> 19:37.761
- I can't let…
- I can't let them overturn the curfew.

19:37.845 --> 19:39.096
…the curfew…

19:59.950 --> 20:01.618
I think they're meeting soon.

20:12.004 --> 20:13.005
You okay?

20:39.948 --> 20:41.658
You're goddamn right we're mad!

20:41.742 --> 20:44.244
We've poured our blood, sweat, tears

20:44.328 --> 20:49.499
and a hell of a lot of money into trying
to make this "the next Martha's Vineyard."

20:49.583 --> 20:51.668
And the crazy thing is, it is working.

20:51.752 --> 20:56.089
It is actually happening,
and you are destroying it for what?

20:57.132 --> 20:58.133
For what?

20:58.217 --> 20:59.551
For what?

20:59.635 --> 21:00.844
For what? For what?

21:05.265 --> 21:09.144
You can't keep people locked indoors
while the sun is still up, Loftis.

21:10.479 --> 21:12.689
People come here for the outdoor stuff.

21:12.773 --> 21:14.525
Beaches and sunshine.

21:14.608 --> 21:18.570
Not to spend all day
in my piece of shit hotel!

21:19.238 --> 21:21.573
It's okay! My piece of shit hotel!

21:21.657 --> 21:23.200
It sucks! I know it sucks!

21:23.784 --> 21:26.328
It's sucked for 25 years!
That's why I don't live there!

21:26.828 --> 21:30.374
I say fuck the moratoriums,

21:30.457 --> 21:32.334
- fuck the curfews.
- Yep.

21:32.417 --> 21:33.961
- I want more tourists.
- I'm ready.

21:34.503 --> 21:37.130
I want more money coming into the island!

21:37.214 --> 21:38.423
- Yes.
- Right.

21:38.507 --> 21:42.594
And we sure as fuck aren't canceling
the fucking fireworks!

21:42.678 --> 21:44.638
That's right! That's right, Kurt!

21:45.806 --> 21:48.350
Hold it! Hold it!

21:48.433 --> 21:49.977
Hold it, hold it!

21:50.060 --> 21:52.855
I wanna hear from Loftis!

21:52.938 --> 21:55.315
Let's hear what he has to say!

22:19.256 --> 22:21.133
Someone's got a full belly.

22:21.884 --> 22:23.260
You had a lot to eat today?

22:26.638 --> 22:27.639
You okay, boss?

22:42.362 --> 22:43.655
There you are!

22:45.032 --> 22:46.491
It's categorically not correct.

22:46.575 --> 22:49.244
- Okay?
- I'm s… I'm serious dude.

22:49.745 --> 22:50.871
It's true.

22:50.954 --> 22:53.498
- It's true, my uncle doesn't lie to me.
- Wait, what is that?

22:53.582 --> 22:54.583
What?

22:56.293 --> 22:58.170
I think I saw something in the window.

23:00.339 --> 23:02.341
I just think you're really high.

23:05.802 --> 23:06.803
It's okay.

23:08.972 --> 23:10.307
Don't worry, I'll protect you.

23:11.141 --> 23:12.518
- Really?
- Yeah.

23:13.018 --> 23:15.771
I'll protect you. Mr. Brave Guy.

23:16.563 --> 23:18.607
- Brave guy.
- Okay. No.

23:19.483 --> 23:21.276
Well, you know, you know what they say.

23:21.944 --> 23:23.570
Anyone that goes in doesn't come out.

23:25.072 --> 23:26.114
I bet you won't.

23:32.037 --> 23:34.831
Oh, my God! Okay.

23:35.791 --> 23:36.792
Let's see it.

23:38.043 --> 23:39.837
Come on, I think that's pretty good.

23:42.089 --> 23:44.591
- He's not gonna do it.
- He's gonna pretend like he's hot shit.

23:44.675 --> 23:45.759
He's gonna like throw himself--

23:47.469 --> 23:48.971
Didn't work on me, didn't work.

23:49.054 --> 23:51.306
- He's gonna be…
- Yes, it did. I saw you jump.

23:51.390 --> 23:52.474
You did.

23:52.558 --> 23:55.143
Come on, buddy. Come on, pal.

23:55.227 --> 23:56.895
- Yeah, there he goes.
- Dude.

23:56.979 --> 23:58.105
- That's right.
- He's still going.

24:01.233 --> 24:06.196
Right? And… Yeah. Sorry
about the math teacher coffee breath.

24:06.280 --> 24:07.823
I didn't catch a whiff.

24:07.906 --> 24:09.575
Good. The… So…

24:10.367 --> 24:12.452
There is… well, there is no year here,

24:12.536 --> 24:15.831
but what caught my interest was
right here.

24:15.914 --> 24:17.708
The reference to a plague.

24:18.709 --> 24:21.545
There's only been one plague
in Widow's Bay and that was in 1702.

24:22.129 --> 24:25.257
So, right, I took a swing.

24:27.843 --> 24:28.844
There it is.

24:34.057 --> 24:35.267
Isn't that something?

24:35.350 --> 24:36.852
Yes, Sarah Westcott Warren.

24:36.935 --> 24:38.145
Where am I?

24:39.313 --> 24:40.606
You seen anything yet?

24:43.192 --> 24:45.235
Okay, well, we're on to something, Tom,

24:45.319 --> 24:47.279
so, just hold on a second.

24:47.362 --> 24:48.780
Use your crayons.

24:48.864 --> 24:50.324
Yeah, and…

24:50.407 --> 24:53.952
She married Richard Warren,
our founding father, that year.

24:54.036 --> 24:57.289
And here, this. This reference here
about the cylinder he wears?

24:57.372 --> 24:58.874
This "cursed" item?

25:00.250 --> 25:01.835
What is this? What does that look like?

25:01.919 --> 25:05.422
Well, if you give me a paintbrush,
I can tell you whatever you need to know.

25:05.506 --> 25:07.716
Yeah, that's great Tom. What is it, Wyck?

25:07.799 --> 25:10.928
I'm wondering if he could've been
buried with it.

25:11.011 --> 25:12.346
The cylinder?

25:13.305 --> 25:15.933
Evan? Ev… Evan? Evan?

25:16.850 --> 25:17.893
Where's my son?

25:20.020 --> 25:22.231
Where's Evan? Where's my son?

25:22.314 --> 25:24.358
- Okay, take it easy.
- Where is Evan?

25:24.441 --> 25:26.693
Just sit down, Tom.

25:26.777 --> 25:27.861
Sit.

25:28.529 --> 25:29.738
Sit.

25:29.821 --> 25:30.989
Down. Sit!

25:31.573 --> 25:33.909
Tom! Tom! Tom!

25:34.493 --> 25:35.494
Tom!

25:39.623 --> 25:40.624
Hey.

25:41.166 --> 25:43.961
Only lap belts back there, buckle up.

25:46.296 --> 25:48.090
I have to find Evan.

25:48.715 --> 25:51.844
Well, I hope he's at your house,

25:51.927 --> 25:54.137
'cause that's where they told me
to take you.

25:54.221 --> 25:55.514
Oh, thank God.

25:55.597 --> 25:57.140
I just need to make one little stop.

25:57.224 --> 26:00.394
- What? No, no, please. No.
- Only gonna take a second.

26:00.477 --> 26:02.020
- No! Rosemary, no!
- One--

26:48.775 --> 26:50.694
Don't move the car again, Tom.

26:52.404 --> 26:56.158
Ha! Just won 15 bucks! Yes!

27:07.586 --> 27:08.962
That's my loafer.

27:10.297 --> 27:11.590
No, no, no!

27:11.673 --> 27:14.426
I told you to get out! Get out!

27:14.927 --> 27:15.969
No, no, no!

28:00.430 --> 28:04.268
Evan Loftis. Please step away
from the creepy house.

28:06.645 --> 28:09.815
This isn't my house? My bad.

28:09.898 --> 28:11.567
- Boy, get over here.
- I…

28:11.650 --> 28:12.651
Thank God.

28:20.242 --> 28:24.204
Hi. I'm sorry.

28:24.288 --> 28:27.666
We have some off-island girls in the car,

28:27.749 --> 28:30.419
and I just… We were just
trying to impress them.

28:32.004 --> 28:33.964
Yeah. Yeah, no, I get it.

28:35.048 --> 28:37.676
Breaking and entering is very impressive.

28:40.137 --> 28:41.889
Please don't tell my dad.

28:44.433 --> 28:47.019
Fine, but go ahead and get outta here.

28:47.102 --> 28:48.520
Okay. Thank you.

28:52.274 --> 28:55.903
Just while I'm walking away, can, I…

28:55.986 --> 28:59.656
Can I just yell "Fuck you, pig"
for the girls?

29:01.867 --> 29:03.410
No, the fuck, you cannot.

29:03.493 --> 29:04.661
Okay. Okay.

29:06.663 --> 29:07.664
Bye.

29:23.472 --> 29:24.473
Oh, shit.

29:37.027 --> 29:38.862
The fuck is going on with your dad, dude?

29:39.404 --> 29:40.489
That's your dad?

29:42.407 --> 29:43.659
What's up? What's up?

29:51.124 --> 29:52.125
Oh, my God.

30:00.092 --> 30:02.386
Yo, I think your dad is looking for you.

30:19.361 --> 30:20.654
- I gotta go. Go.
- Okay.

30:21.154 --> 30:24.032
Get inside, right now.
And say good night to little…

30:25.742 --> 30:26.743
miss.

30:30.080 --> 30:31.790
You better start explaining yourself
right--

30:31.874 --> 30:33.500
- Fuck you!
- What did you say?

30:34.001 --> 30:35.919
What did you… What did you just say?

30:43.260 --> 30:44.761
I had fun tonight.

30:45.554 --> 30:46.930
I had a good time.

30:49.558 --> 30:52.644
And if you had it your way, I would've sat
in your shitty office all day.

30:52.728 --> 30:54.646
Evan, do you think I want to be

30:54.730 --> 30:56.940
- watching you the whole fucking time?
- No, I don't!

30:57.024 --> 31:00.444
No, I think you wanna show people
that you can control me.

31:01.361 --> 31:02.362
What?

31:04.865 --> 31:08.785
The reason you're a shitty mayor
is not because of me, okay?

31:16.376 --> 31:18.754
I think… I think… I think

31:18.837 --> 31:20.380
you're gonna feel very guilty

31:20.464 --> 31:22.132
for saying that to me one day.

31:26.970 --> 31:28.555
Why do we never leave this island?

31:32.935 --> 31:34.436
What kind of fucking parenting is that?

31:34.520 --> 31:36.939
It was important to your mother
that you be raised here.

31:37.022 --> 31:38.815
What? Never go anywhere?
That's what she wanted?

31:38.899 --> 31:40.234
We'll continue this in the morning.

31:45.280 --> 31:46.281
Dad!

31:47.157 --> 31:48.158
Dad!

31:48.242 --> 31:51.995
Dad, one of these days, I'm gonna leave
and I'm never, ever coming back!

32:26.196 --> 32:27.197
Are you ready?

32:29.157 --> 32:30.200
Are you ready?

32:33.203 --> 32:34.204
Are you ready?

32:45.632 --> 32:47.426
Lauren? Lauren? Lauren?

32:58.228 --> 32:59.229
I can't see anything.

33:02.983 --> 33:06.111
Lauren? Lauren?

33:07.529 --> 33:10.449
- Lauren? Lauren?
- I can't see anything!

33:10.532 --> 33:11.617
I can't see anything!

33:11.700 --> 33:13.660
I need some help here, please!

33:13.744 --> 33:16.705
Can you please turn the boat around?
Turn the boat around.

33:16.788 --> 33:18.123
Turn it now! Now!

33:18.207 --> 33:19.917
Lauren? Lauren?

33:26.089 --> 33:27.716
The baby is just fine.

33:29.218 --> 33:32.054
Okay. But what about her?

33:32.137 --> 33:33.514
She… She seems…

33:34.890 --> 33:35.974
off.

33:36.558 --> 33:38.185
Just give it some time.

33:42.731 --> 33:43.732
Hello.

34:04.044 --> 34:09.257
Please, oh, God, if you can hear me,

34:10.092 --> 34:11.885
if you exist…

34:14.429 --> 34:16.348
please help me.

34:17.474 --> 34:18.641
Please. Please help me.

34:18.725 --> 34:20.768
Please, please protect my son.

34:23.355 --> 34:25.023
Please protect my son.

34:28.235 --> 34:29.610
I'll do anything.
